From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: complete NPU BA retirement before reuse

The RRO session worker acknowledges a BA deletion to WM even when the
NPU signature-clear request fails. WM may then reuse a session whose
old signature entries remain visible. An uncertain WM acknowledgment
also cannot safely be retried against a possibly reused session id.

Wait in process context for the owned NPU request and require its
successful completion before sending the WM deletion. Retain failed
and unprocessed notifications behind a persistent gate, then request a
full recovery asynchronously. Keep both requests and their receipts
separate from atomic mailbox users.

After NPU drain, endpoint DMA quiescence and Wi-Fi firmware reload,
invalidate the signatures of every normal and special RRO session with
the existing per-session callback. Preserve the address, head, count,
bitmap and base registrations instead of repeating cold initialization.
Share one absolute 30-second deadline across all 1025 original requests.
Keep NPU workers and RRO NAPI stopped until every clear succeeds, before
RRO configuration and NPU resume. Record the completed count, elapsed
time and failing SID without retrying an uncertain request. Stop without
NPU resume on failure; reconcile the notification ledger only after the
complete restart succeeds. Free host-only event records after producer
shutdown; their addresses are never submitted to either firmware.

Consume full-reset requests under the recovery lock before each
attempt, preserving a new request that arrives while recovery runs.
Keep failed attempts pending without introducing an unbounded retry.

Fixes: d7a79fcece87 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: Integrate NPU in RRO session management")
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
